# Clippy warning baseline — ratcheted gate (issue #3999).
#
# One line per individual `warning:` from
# `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` (cargo's per-target
# "generated N warnings" summaries excluded):
#   <warning text> <TAB> <file>
# Lines are sorted; duplicates are preserved. The gate's count is
# the number of non-comment lines below.
#
# Consumers(config/clippy-warnings.baseline): scripts/clippy-baseline.sh
#
# Regenerate only downward:
#   bash scripts/clippy-baseline.sh --rebaseline
# refuses to record a higher count; a change that raises this
# baseline is a review rejection, not a rebaseline.
#
# Carve-out tracked as a SEPARATE issue (not baselined away as
# lint noise): the dead-code findings (`function ... is never
# used`, `struct ... is never constructed`) are correctness
# signals — see the follow-up issue filed from #3999.
#
# Last rebaseline: 2026-09-10 (1022 warnings)
